WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.119
Geometric Alignment without
Functional Equivalence:

00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:07.740
a layer-wise analysis of the
speech-text modality gap.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.353
Ask a speech language model the same
question, once as text and once as speech.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.109
From text, it answers correctly.
From speech, it does not.

00:00:24.409 --> 00:00:31.852
Across four models and two benchmarks,
speech is less accurate. On BBH,

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:36.569
Qwen2.5-Omni drops from 72.7 to 59.9 percent.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:41.087
A common view studies this gap through geometry:

00:00:41.087 --> 00:00:45.308
how close do speech representations
get to text inside the model?

00:00:45.608 --> 00:00:48.803
Comparing every speech
layer with every text layer,

00:00:48.803 --> 00:00:52.499
speech and text align in a
broad band in the middle layers.

00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:57.561
But alignment does not mean the
model uses speech the same way.

00:00:57.861 --> 00:01:02.622
Layer by layer, we track how strongly
the model prefers the correct answer.

00:01:02.622 --> 00:01:05.605
The margins split apart in the last six layers.

00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:10.343
And whichever input gets the answer
right holds the larger margin there.

00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:17.749
At the moment of answering, attention over
text concentrates on a few tokens. Over speech,

00:01:17.749 --> 00:01:18.891
it is spread thin.

00:01:19.191 --> 00:01:25.719
In late layers, speech needs 3.7 times as many
tokens to hold 90 percent of the attention.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.706
With the input held fixed,

00:01:27.706 --> 00:01:33.613
sharpening late speech attention increases
answer separation in all four conditions tested.

00:01:35.313 --> 00:01:37.980
Across models, the gap takes two forms.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:44.674
Qwen2.5-Omni and MiniCPM-o align in the
middle, but decide differently late.

00:01:44.674 --> 00:01:48.797
Qwen2-Audio never aligns well in the first place.

00:01:49.097 --> 00:01:52.749
So repairs should target late
answer formation in one case,

00:01:52.749 --> 00:01:55.348
and representation formation in the other.

00:01:57.048 --> 00:02:00.397
Geometric alignment is not functional equivalence.
